kbuild: a function order for vmlinux, as a list of symbols for lld

make KERNEL_ORDER=<file> passes the file to ld.lld as
--symbol-ordering-file. With full LTO, lld puts every function in its own
section, so the listed functions come first in .text, in this order;
names that the kernel does not have are skipped without a warning.

v86 compiles guest code per page of 4 KiB: a page gets a JIT module once
it ran enough instructions, and a module ends at every jump into another
page. In the normal link order, 90 % of the kernel instructions of a pod
start are spread over ~100-130 pages; vm/kernel-order.txt (made with
korder.cjs of tools/pod-bench in jkroepke/v86) puts the hot functions that
call each other on the same pages. vm/kernel-order.md explains it, and how
to check and renew the order after a kernel upgrade.

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 05c5b682a..bad57f2ef 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -1262,6 +1262,11 @@ ifdef CONFIG_LD_ORPHAN_WARN
 LDFLAGS_vmlinux += --orphan-handling=$(CONFIG_LD_ORPHAN_WARN_LEVEL)
 endif
 
+# The order of the functions in .text: make KERNEL_ORDER=<file> (lld)
+ifdef KERNEL_ORDER
+LDFLAGS_vmlinux += --symbol-ordering-file=$(KERNEL_ORDER) --no-warn-symbol-ordering
+endif
+
 ifneq ($(CONFIG_ARCH_VMLINUX_NEEDS_RELOCS),)
 LDFLAGS_vmlinux	+= --emit-relocs --discard-none
 endif
